        "script": "Why is content not working now? Well, when the niche gets saturated, imagine there's like a red line that starts at the bottom and like slowly starts rising up that pyramid. If you're below the line, you're fucked because that means there's way too many people making these like generic commoditized formats. There's a lot of people in many niches making this like fact -based list -based stuff that has no insight. New people come in and they think that's the way to do it. They're below the red line, they're flopping. What you need to do is get above that red line. So as things get competitive, that red line will slowly increase where it's gonna eat all the fact -based formats where there'll be no alpha and it will leave you with only application and stories."
